# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Nothing here is secret — see the warning further
# down for the things that are.
#
# ─── How the two halves of this project get configured ───────────────────────
#
# There are exactly two families of variable, they live in different places, and
# confusing them is the one mistake with real consequences:
#
#   1. VITE_* — read by the browser apps. Vite INLINES these into the JavaScript
#      bundle at build time, so every value below is served to the public. That
#      is fine for what is here, and fatal for anything else. Never put an API
#      key behind a VITE_ prefix; the prefix means "publish this".
#
#      For the deployed site these are set as BUILD variables in Cloudflare
#      (Workers & Pages → abdash-labs → Settings → Build), not runtime secrets —
#      a runtime secret arrives after the bundle is already written.
#
#   2. Everything else — read by the Supabase Edge Functions, server-side, and
#      set with `supabase secrets set`. They never appear in a .env consumed by
#      this repo and never reach the browser. Listed at the bottom for
#      reference only.
#
# A missing VITE_ variable does NOT fail the build. The build succeeds and the
# browser throws `Missing required environment variable: VITE_SUPABASE_URL` on
# first paint, so check the console before suspecting anything subtler.


# ─── Required: the apps that talk to Supabase ────────────────────────────────
# Recto, AskSheet, Critiq, RAG Lab and GraphRead all need these. PlaneMode does
# not — it runs its model in the browser and imports no Supabase code at all,
# which is the whole point of it.

# Project → Settings → API → Project URL
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Project → Settings → API Keys → publishable key (`sb_publishable_…`).
# Prefer it over the legacy `anon` JWT: same access, rotates independently.
# This key is meant to be public. Row-level security is the actual boundary —
# every table is scoped to `owner_id = auth.uid()`, and tests/rls/ exists to
# prove a second user cannot read the first user's rows.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key_here


# ─── Optional: captcha ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave this UNSET unless Supabase Auth captcha protection is switched on.
#
# The two settings are coupled and must agree. With no site key, AuthGate signs
# in anonymously the moment the app loads. With one, it waits for a Turnstile
# token first. Turn captcha on in Supabase but forget the key here and every app
# hangs on "Setting up your workspace…" forever, because the widget that would
# produce the token never renders.
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=


# ─── NOT set here: Supabase Edge Function secrets ────────────────────────────
# Server-side only. Set with `supabase secrets set NAME=value`, never in this
# file, and never with a VITE_ prefix — that would publish them to every visitor.
#
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY   All chat and vision calls. `OPENROUTER_KEY` also works.
#   OPENAI_API_KEY       Embeddings only — OpenRouter has no embeddings endpoint.
#   CONCIERGE_IP_SALT    Salts hashed IPs for the Concierge's rate limit, so the
#                        stored value cannot be reversed into a visitor's IP.
#                        Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
#   MODEL_CHEAP          Optional. Overrides the small model used for GraphRead
#                        extraction and AskSheet planning; falls back if unset.
#   RAGLAB_RUN_SECRET    Optional. HMAC key material for RAG Lab run tokens.
#                        Falls back to the service-role key, then to a dev
#                        constant — set it explicitly in production.
#
# SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are injected
# into every Edge Function by the platform. Do not set them by hand.
